  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming data transparency in clean power supply chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the launch of Global Clean Power Alliance (GCPA) at COP29 in Baku, the UK Government is working on preparing the implementation phase of the GCPA. A priority for implementation will be the GCPA Supply Chain Mission, a two-year activity to discuss among government officials the risks posed to supply chains for clean energy technologies, along with potential ways to mitigate these risks. 
The GCPA Supply Chains Mission will consist of four pillars: 1) Data 2) Sectoral collaboration 3) Circularity 4) EMDEs. This project will cover the data pillar, which will involve working with the International Energy Agency to identify challenges with respect to the accuracy, granularity and timeliness of data on supply chains, along with proposals on how to improve the quantity and quality of data going forward. The aim of the Data pillar is to improve global quality, access and transparency of data on clean energy supply chains for better evidence-based policy-making (not limited to supply chains for the power sector).</narrative>
  </description>
